# Build artifacts. paper.pdf used to be tracked so a reader could get the
# manuscript without a Typst install. It is not any more: git keeps every version
# of a binary forever, a clone pays for all of them, and removing one means
# rewriting history. Ship the PDF as a release asset or a CI artifact instead.
#
# Staleness is answered without git now -- `just paper` and `just docx` record
# the hash of what they rendered in .build-stamp and `just check-build` recompares
# it. .build-stamp is untracked too, because it describes local build output:
# tracking it would let a rebuild here report every other checkout stale.
paper.pdf
paper-draft.pdf
.build-stamp
# Stat-keyed cache for the content hashes `just verify` compares. Local build
# state like .build-stamp: safe to delete, never the recorded truth (that stays
# in stats.json / assets.json). See tools/hashcache.py.
.hash-cache.json
# Snapshot of paper.pdf's extracted text, for `just text-diff` around a
# structural refactor. Local and disposable, like the build stamp.
.text-baseline
# Snapshots of the manuscript's mechanical properties (numbers, refs, floats,
# headings), for `just edit-check` around a copy-edit pass. Same contract.
.edit-guard/

# Rendered from stats.json by tools/render_stats.py: the display strings Typst
# reads. Derived, not source -- stats.json holds the value and the format spec,
# and this is what Python's formatter makes of them. Every recipe that compiles
# regenerates it, so it is never stale and never worth committing.
stats-rendered.json
# just viz diagnostics: regenerated on demand, never part of the manuscript
viz/
paper.docx
paper.docx.html

# Audio toolchain: voice models and every generated audio file. The engine is a
# uv dependency now (piper-tts), so there is no downloaded binary to ignore.
# Only the scripts in audio/ are tracked, so a fresh clone runs `just audio-setup`.
audio/models/
audio/.venv/
audio/chapters/
audio/chapters_si/
audio/*.wav
audio/*.mp3
audio/*.opus
audio/*.m4b
audio/paper_prose.txt
audio/cover_main.png
audio/cover_si.png

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Analysis inputs and intermediates. The CODE in analysis/ is tracked; the heavy
# data and the results tree are not, and neither is its virtualenv. The generated
# figures/ and si/ ARE tracked, so a fresh clone compiles the PDF without
# re-running an analysis that may take hours.
analysis/data/
analysis/results/
analysis/.venv/
